== Description
<description-2>
#emph[Requested by #strong[Sia] ·
#link("https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2CeT7EXLucCBx8drQGW8YWR")[project thread]]

Before: there was no place to track code issues, and working on a
dotfiles branch meant checking it out in #raw(lang:"verbatim", "~"),
which swaps the live config.

After: #raw(lang:"verbatim", "M-x sp-org-issues-create-area") creates an
\"Issues\" file as a vulpea-para area (tagged
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "area"), in the vulpea database), with one heading
per repository (dotfiles, vulpea-mcp). #raw(lang:"verbatim", "C-c c I")
files an issue under a repository, #raw(lang:"verbatim", "C-c o a i i")
shows an issue board (in progress, next, waiting, open), and
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "M-x sp-org-issues-start") gives an issue its own
git worktree under #raw(lang:"verbatim", "~/src/dotfiles-wt/") and opens
Magit there. For the dotfiles the worktree is added from the yadm
repository itself, so #raw(lang:"verbatim", "~") is never touched.

How: the file sets the org-gtd keywords
(#raw(lang:"verbatim", "TODO NEXT PROG WAIT | DONE CNCL")) with its own
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "#+todo:") line, and every issue carries
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "ORG_GTD: Actions"), so a NEXT issue also shows in
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "org-gtd-engage"). Repository settings
(#raw(lang:"verbatim", "GIT_DIR"),
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "WORKTREE_ROOT"), #raw(lang:"verbatim", "BASE"))
sit on the repository heading and are inherited by the issues. The
module requires #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-vulpea-para") first and
appends its capture template and agenda commands, so that module\'s
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "setq") cannot wipe them. Closing an issue offers
to remove its worktree, and Magit lists untracked files in yadm
worktrees (the yadm repo hides them for #raw(lang:"verbatim", "~")).
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "init.el") loads it right after
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-org-ext").

The literate source is
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "docs/tangles/sp-org-issues.org")\; it tangles
back to the #raw(lang:"verbatim", ".el") byte for byte. Tested in batch
Emacs with Org and current Magit against a repository laid out like
yadm\'s (vulpea calls stubbed): area creation, capture into an existing
and a missing repository heading, both agenda views, starting an issue
from the agenda (branch, worktree, PROG), and removing the worktree on
DONE.

