Before: there was no file tree in the config, so keeping the modules and
the docs in #raw(lang:"verbatim", "docs/tangles") in view meant
switching to dired.

After: pressing #raw(lang:"verbatim", "\u{3c}f9>") opens a treemacs side
window rooted at #raw(lang:"verbatim", "~/.config/emacs-modular")
(#raw(lang:"verbatim", "user-emacs-directory")), and pressing it again
closes it. Nothing opens at startup.

The tree is rooted at a fixed folder,
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-treemacs-root"), instead of treemacs\'
\"current project\", because the yadm repository\'s root is
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "\u{24}HOME") and following the project would show the
whole home folder.

How: a new module,
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "libraries/modules/ui/sp-treemacs.el"), installs
treemacs through Elpaca (#raw(lang:"verbatim", ":ensure t")), binds
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "\u{3c}f9>") to
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-treemacs-toggle"), keeps treemacs\' saved
workspace in #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-cache-dir"), and turns on
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "treemacs-follow-mode"). The toggle is defined in
#raw(lang:"verbatim", ":config") because it uses the
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "treemacs-is-path") macro. The module is added to
the window management group in #raw(lang:"verbatim", "init.el"), after
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-mini-frame"). Its literate doc,
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "docs/tangles/sp-treemacs.org"), tangles back to
the #raw(lang:"verbatim", ".el") byte for byte (checked with
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "org-babel-tangle-file")), and has a
#raw(lang:"verbatim", ":tangle no") Sandbox block.

Tested in #raw(lang:"verbatim", "emacs -nw -Q") with treemacs from
source: #raw(lang:"verbatim", "\u{3c}f9>") is an autoload before first use,
the first press adds the root and shows the tree, the second hides it,
the third shows it again without adding the root twice.

