Before: discourse-graphs could tell me a claim was contested only
through its own dashboards, its status logic was fixed, and the
research-question states I had sketched had one catch-all
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "CONTESTED") state.

After: a new #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-dg-positions") module draws the
positions in a discourse graph the way
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-vulpea-hierarchy") draws the note hierarchy,
with the same kind of interface
(#raw(lang:"verbatim", "dg-positions-outline"),
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "dg-positions-graph"),
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "dg-positions-rankdir"),
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "dg-positions-graph-file")). It adds one view per
status (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "dg-positions-status")), a gaps view and a
check view. Questions, claims, evidence and sources, the relations
between them, the statuses and the gaps are all declared in one readable
list, #raw(lang:"verbatim", "dg-positions-rules"), so a new relation
such as #raw(lang:"verbatim", "contests") or
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "reframes") is one line. A new doc,
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "docs/tangles/research-question-states.org"), says
exactly which state each object should be in; how contested an answer is
now lives on the answer, not on the question.

How: the module reads #raw(lang:"verbatim", "dg-all-nodes") and
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "dg-all-relations") from the discourse-graphs
database and never writes to a note.
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "dg-positions-install") copies the declared node
types and relations into discourse-graphs\' own variables so it parses
the new #raw(lang:"verbatim", "DG_\u{3c}RELATION>") properties; run
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "dg-rebuild-cache") afterwards. The literate doc
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "docs/tangles/custom/sp-dg-positions.org") is the
source and tangles to
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "libraries/modules/custom/sp-dg-positions.el")\;
it is loaded from #raw(lang:"verbatim", "init.el") after
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-vulpea-hierarchy"). The doc\'s nine ERT tests
pass in Emacs batch mode, the file byte-compiles without warnings, and
the graph was rendered with Graphviz. It has not been run against a real
discourse-graphs database.

