#strong[Before:] #raw(lang:"verbatim", "relationship-annotator-graph")
wrote a static HTML file and opened it from disk, so the graph was a
snapshot and needed a new run after every edit.

#strong[After:]

- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "M-x rel-anno-graph") now opens a live view: a
  new module #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-relationship-annotator-live")
  serves the same page from Emacs on
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "http://127.0.0.1:8765/"), rendered from the
  vulpea database on each load. The old static command is
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "rel-anno-graph-static") (unchanged otherwise,
  and the SVG export is untouched). Also
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "rel-anno-live-open"),
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "-start"), #raw(lang:"verbatim", "-stop"),
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "-refresh")\; options
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "relationship-annotator-live-port") and
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "-debounce").
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "/graph.json") returns the nodes and edges.
- #strong[Shorter command prefix.] All interactive commands use
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "rel-anno-")
  (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "rel-anno-svg"),
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "rel-anno-review"),
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "rel-anno-outline-native"),
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "rel-anno-outline-vui"), the three
  outline-buffer commands and the live ones). #strong[The obsolete
  aliases are removed], including the old
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "vulpea-hierarchy-*") ones, so the old command
  names no longer work; nothing else in the repo used them. Variables
  and internal functions keep the long prefix.
- #strong[No polling.] An open page holds a Server-Sent Events stream.
  Emacs watches the folder of
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "vulpea-db-location") with
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "file-notify"), waits until it is idle
  (debounced), cuts the tree for each open page and compares a SHA-1 of
  the data with the one the page was rendered from. Only a different
  hash sends a message, so editing a note that is not in the graph
  reloads nothing. A page that reconnects after a drop is compared the
  same way, so changes made meanwhile are not lost.
- On a reload the page restores the note it was recentred on, pan, zoom
  and folded branches (kept in #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sessionStorage")).

#strong[How:] a small server on
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "make-network-process"), bound to 127.0.0.1 (not
configurable), GET only, rejecting any #raw(lang:"verbatim", "Host")
header that is not localhost with this port. I did not use
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "simple-httpd") (one global server rooted at
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "/var/www"), all interfaces by default). On
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "vulpea-graph"): the analysis found no rendering
code to reuse (metrics and lists only), so only its neighbour-walk idea
applies, already done by
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "relationship-annotator--scope")\; I did not read
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "vulpea-graph-ui"). Literate doc in
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "docs/tangles/custom/sp-relationship-annotator-live.org")\;
the annotator doc and #raw(lang:"verbatim", "docs/main.org") are
updated; #raw(lang:"verbatim", "init.el") loads the module after
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-relationship-annotator")\;
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "CHANGELOG.org") entries added.

#strong[Tested] (Emacs 29.3, in a container, real annotator code with
stubbed vulpea/vui and three fake notes): the modules tangle from their
docs and byte-compile. A batch Emacs served #raw(lang:"verbatim", "/"),
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "/graph.json"),
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "/favicon.ico"), 404, 403 (wrong Host or port),
405 (POST). With an event stream open: a db file touch without a data
change sent nothing; a title change plus a touch sent
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "changed")\; a stale
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "since") hash on connect and
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "-refresh") sent it; a closed stream was dropped;
stop closed everything. Headless Chromium on a live server: the page
drew, a recentre plus pan and zoom survived a data-triggered reload, no
JS errors.

#strong[Not tested:] real vulpea (whether
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "vulpea-db-autosync-mode") writes
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "vulpea-db-location") or its
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "-wal") soon after a save, and that name being
right on your version), your vault and its size (a check builds the tree
in Emacs while idle), macOS file notification (fsevents/kqueue), the
idle timer in an interactive Emacs (batch has none; the test used a
plain timer), the outline buffer keys and the vui outline (not run),
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "browse-url") with your browser. If the watch
cannot start, a message says so and
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "rel-anno-live-refresh") remains.

