#strong[After:] new module #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-org-normalise")
(#raw(lang:"verbatim", "libraries/modules/custom/"), literate doc
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "docs/tangles/custom/sp-org-normalise.org"),
listed in #raw(lang:"verbatim", "docs/main.org"), loaded from
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "init.el") after
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-org-issues")).

- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "M-x sp-org-normalise-inventory"): every
  keyword-like heading word with heading and file counts, how many files
  do not recognise it, and what the mapping table does with it.
- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "M-x sp-org-normalise-preview"): report buffer
  of proposed changes per file; #raw(lang:"verbatim", "RET") visits a
  change. Writes nothing.
- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "M-x sp-org-normalise-run"): the preview, then
  per file yes / no / choose each change / quit. Buffers are left
  modified and unsaved
  (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-org-normalise-save-after-apply") to
  change).
- Checkbox items under a #raw(lang:"verbatim", "Tasks") heading become
  child headings: #raw(lang:"verbatim", "[ ]") TODO,
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "[X]") DONE, #raw(lang:"verbatim", "[-]") PROG.
  Nested lines stay in the body. A checklist under a heading that
  already has a keyword is left alone.
- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-org-normalise-keyword-map") (editable)
  rewrites #raw(lang:"verbatim", "DOING"),
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "WAITING"), #raw(lang:"verbatim", "CANCELLED"),
  … to the org-gtd set; words not in it are only reported. A
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "#+todo:") line is proposed for files that would
  otherwise use an unknown keyword; files with their own sequence are
  only noted.
- Code blocks and drawers are never read. All
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "defcustom=s are in the group =sp-org-normalise").
