==== What it does
<what-it-does>
- #strong[#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-tag-emoji")]
  (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "libraries/modules/custom/")):
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-tag-emoji-rules") maps a tag, or a list of
  tags that must all be present, to #raw(lang:"verbatim", ":emoji")
  and/or #raw(lang:"verbatim", ":face") (and
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", ":position") prefix/suffix for links).
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-tag-emoji-mode") shows the tags of the
  heading at point, or the file\'s #raw(lang:"verbatim", "#+filetags:"),
  as emoji in the modeline (or header line), and decorates
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "id:") links with the emoji and face of the tags
  of their note, read from the vulpea db. A combination rule uses up its
  tags, so #raw(lang:"verbatim", "(\"\u{40}writing\" \"deep\")") replaces the
  two single emoji. #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-tag-emoji-check-rules")
  lists rule tags missing from #raw(lang:"verbatim", "org-tag-alist"),
  so that stays the single tag registry.
- #strong[#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-emoji-font")]
  (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "libraries/modules/ui/")): prepends the first
  installed colour emoji family (Apple Color Emoji, then Noto Color
  Emoji, …) to the #raw(lang:"verbatim", "emoji") fontset. On Linux,
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-emoji-font-file") or
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "M-x sp-emoji-font-install") installs an Apple
  Color Emoji #raw(lang:"verbatim", ".ttf") into
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "~/.local/share/fonts/sp-emoji/"). The font is
  not bundled (Apple\'s licence).
- Literate docs in
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "docs/tangles/custom/sp-tag-emoji.org") and
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "docs/tangles/ui/sp-emoji-font.org")\;
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "init.el"),
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "docs/main.org") and CHANGELOG follow.

==== Checked (Emacs 29.3, headless, container)
<checked-emacs-293-headless-container>
Both docs tangle; the rules, the combo logic, the heading/file/both
sources, inheritance, the modeline string, the header-line placement,
