#raw(lang:"verbatim", "main") after \#59 merges.

#strong[Before:] notes written with Org\'s default behaviour end in a
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "Footnotes") heading, but this setup keeps each
definition at the end of the text of the heading that cites it
(#raw(lang:"verbatim", "org-footnote-section") is nil;
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-vulpea-split") copies definitions per
heading).

#strong[After:] #raw(lang:"verbatim", "M-x sp-org-lint-footnotes") in
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-org-lint") (docs:
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "docs/tangles/funct/sp-org-lint.org"), \"Sectional
footnotes\").

- #strong[Async:] the files of the vulpea database are read by a second
  headless Emacs (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "make-process")), one at a time;
  a report buffer fills in as results arrive. Emacs stays usable.
- #strong[Preview first:] the scan changes nothing.
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "a") in the report applies, after a yes/no
  question.
- #strong[What moves:] each definition in a
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "Footnotes") heading goes to the end of the own
  text of the heading that contains its reference (same section meaning
  as #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-split--fn-section")). Cited from several
  sections: every section gets a copy, later ones with a suffixed label
  (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "smith-2")), as in
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-vulpea-split"). An emptied
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "Footnotes") heading is removed; one with other
  content stays.
- #strong[Reported, never deleted:] orphan definitions, dangling
  references, and conflicts (label defined twice, cited from the
  footnotes heading itself, cited only from another footnote).
- #strong[Safety:] every file is copied to
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-org-lint-fn-backup-directory") (per-run
  folder) before being written; a file that changed since the preview,
  is open with unsaved edits, has CRLFs, or fails the post-check
  (reference count, dangling set and definition count) is skipped.
  Written via temp file and rename. Open unmodified buffers are reverted
  and vulpea is asked to re-read the files when idle.
- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "C-u") asks for a folder instead of using the
  vulpea database. No external packages.

