+ #raw(lang:"verbatim", "C-c v p") previews the merge in memory with
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "git merge-tree --write-tree") and lists
  conflicting files; #raw(lang:"verbatim", "RET") on one opens a
  three-way Ediff (INTO, FROM, merge base).
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "C-c v d") shows what FROM adds,
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "C-c v e") picks any file for the same Ediff.
+ #raw(lang:"verbatim", "C-c v n") starts a
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "--no-commit") merge (after asking, and after
  offering to check out INTO\'s branch if the worktree is clean). Then
  resolve with Magit #raw(lang:"verbatim", "e"), Smerge or
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "M"), commit with #raw(lang:"verbatim", "c c"),
  or abort with #raw(lang:"verbatim", "m a").

Only step 4 changes the worktree. Nothing commits.

