<description-86>
#emph[Requested by #strong[Sia] ·
#link("https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW23eddj9am1nebvkG14YLgqW")[project thread]]

​\#85 started #raw(lang:"verbatim", "cursor-intangible-mode") from an
idle timer, but the echo-area error still appeared constantly. This
removes the mode.

#strong[Why the error cannot be suppressed]

- The mode puts #raw(lang:"verbatim", "cursor-sensor--move-to-tangible")
  on #raw(lang:"verbatim", "pre-redisplay-functions"). It calls
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "cursor-sensor-tangible-pos"), which returns nil
  when it finds no tangible position, then does arithmetic on nil:
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "(wrong-type-argument number-or-marker-p nil)")
  (Sia\'s backtrace).
- Redisplay runs the hook inside
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "with-demoted-errors"), so the error is caught
  and printed in C-level redisplay before any handler of ours runs.
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "condition-case"),
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "debug-on-error") and
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "warning-suppress-types") cannot reach it.
  Advising the function would mean patching Emacs\'s own code.
- It repeats because redisplay runs the hook every time, for as long as
  the condition holds.
- Edge cases where the mode would work: a buffer that is never erased,
  never redrawn and always has a button. The dashboard redraws on every
  window-state change (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-dashboard-refresh")),
  and the buttons come and go with the privacy mode and agenda boxes, so
  it cannot meet that. A guard that makes it safe would have to run
  before redisplay, which is the same hook.

#strong[Changes] (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-dashboard.el"),
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-dashboard.org"),
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "CHANGELOG.org"))

- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-dashboard--isolate-menu") no longer marks
  text #raw(lang:"verbatim", "cursor-intangible") or starts the mode;
