<description-128>
#emph[Requested by #strong[Sia] ·
#link("https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2XYC9n7jY4gV3tnop2oYDSv")[project thread]]

==== Problem
<problem>
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "M-x sp-split-leave-parents") failed with
\"Autoloading file …/org/org.elc failed to define function
sp-split-leave-parents\".

==== Cause
<cause>
In #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-org-base.el"),
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "(use-package org :bind (:map org-mode-map (\"C-x s t\" . sp-split-leave-parents)))")
makes use-package autoload the command from
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "org"), which does not define it. Until
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-split-leave-parents.el") is loaded (it is only
required by #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-vulpea-ext")), the stub points at
the wrong file.

==== Fix
<fix>
Declare
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "(autoload 'sp-split-leave-parents \"sp-split-leave-parents\" nil t)")
before the #raw(lang:"verbatim", "use-package org") block. use-package
only adds its own autoload when the function is not already bound, so
the correct one wins and the key binding is unchanged. Doc and CHANGELOG
updated.

==== Verification
<verification>
Not run in Emacs (none in the sandbox). I read the code only; please
check #raw(lang:"verbatim", "C-x s t") and
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "M-x sp-split-leave-parents") in a fresh Emacs. If
the error persists,
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "M-x describe-function sp-split-leave-parents")
will show which file the stub names.

