== Description
<description-152>
#emph[Requested by #strong[Sia] ·
#link("https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2VvsAv9bMnVw5hmscGggixs")[project thread]]

==== What
<what>
After \#152, #raw(lang:"verbatim", "M-x") was fine at init but glitched
again once Org was in use. The dimming remapped every face with a
foreground (over a thousand, from #raw(lang:"verbatim", "face-list")) in
each buffer behind the posframe. Every redisplay of that buffer looks
faces up in that remap list, so a busy Org buffer (indent, numbering,
tables, tag groups) redraws slowly on each keystroke in the posframe.

#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-posframe-dim") now remaps
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "default") and the faces found on the visible text
only (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-posframe--visible-faces"), a walk of the
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "face") property from
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "window-start") to
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "window-end")). The look is the same; text
scrolled into view while the minibuffer is open is not dimmed.

The doc has two extra checks for the mirrored-buffer symptom: whether
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "vertico-buffer-mode") is on at the same time as
the posframe, and
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "(setq sp-posframe-dim-always nil)") to rule the
dimming out.

