== Description
<description-170>
#emph[Requested by #strong[Sia] ·
#link("https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2SnxWxFd1BzigKY2tZa4GJe")[project thread]]

A query table can now be sorted by several columns, applied in the order
they are set.

#strong[How I read the request:] \"sort a column based on multiple
parameters, set in order\" as a primary sort key plus tie-breakers (like
a spreadsheet\'s multi-level sort), each with its own direction.

- #raw(lang:"verbatim", ":sort-by") may be a list of columns: the first
  is the primary key, each next one breaks ties of those before it. An
  element may be #raw(lang:"verbatim", "(COLUMN . asc)") or
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "(COLUMN . desc)")\; plain columns use
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", ":sort-desc"). A single column still works.
- The sort is stable, so ties keep the query order (before, descending
  reversed them too).
- Menu: #raw(lang:"verbatim", "o") reads the columns in order
  (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "rating,title:desc"));
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "O") is the default direction for columns
  without their own.
- vui: clicking a column makes it primary and keeps the earlier clicks
  as tie-breakers (the number after the arrow is the rank); a Reset
  button returns to the spec\'s sort.
- exc and Org renderers, the dynamic block and saved views take the list
  through the spec; the summary line says \"sorted by …\". exc\'s own
  in-grid sorting is not touched.
- New #raw(lang:"verbatim", "tests/sp-collection-query-tables-test.el")
  (core sort with stubbed Vulpea, passes on Emacs 29.3). Menu and vui
  were not run in Emacs.
- Literate doc and CHANGELOG updated. Based on main after \#169.

