== Description
<description-173>
#emph[Requested by #strong[Sia] ·
#link("https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2DtCMR6qcoYVuswMQFkPCKF")[project thread]]

Follow-up to \#173 for #raw(lang:"verbatim", "rel-anno-fa2").

- #strong[Room between nodes:] graph-fa2 lays nodes out without knowing
  label sizes, so labels overlapped. Nodes are now drawn
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "relationship-annotator-fa2-spread") (4) times
  farther apart on a canvas that many times larger (advice on
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "graph-fa2-normalise-coords") and its inverse,
  so drag and click still match). Labels keep their size, so zoom in to
  read. The engine is now #raw(lang:"verbatim", "2d"): in 3d, nodes
  behind each other overlap whatever the spacing.
- #strong[Box behind each label:] a rounded box in the node\'s colour at
  75% opacity
  (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "relationship-annotator-fa2-box-opacity")); the
  text takes the theme foreground or background, whichever contrasts.
  graph-fa2 has no box option, so this post-processes its SVG (advice on
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "graph-fa2--render-svg")). I chose the box over
  making the box the node, because the circle still gives the layout and
  click target.
- #strong[Theme colours:] the node fill is the foreground of a theme
  face per tag group colour
  (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "relationship-annotator-fa2-group-faces"):
  orange is #raw(lang:"verbatim", "warning"), green is
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "success"), gray is
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "shadow"), …), and text, edge labels and edges
  follow #raw(lang:"verbatim", "default") and
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "shadow"). It reads the theme each time the
  command runs.

Tested in headless Emacs 29 with the real graph-fa2: the SVG gets the
boxes, and across 12 to 60 boxes (2d), overlapping pairs went from 6 to
33 at spread 1 to none at spread 4. In 3d some still overlapped, hence
the 2d engine. Not seen on screen: how the colours look on your themes
and the zoom level. Literate doc and CHANGELOG updated.

