==== What
<what>
The query tables
(#raw(lang:"verbatim", "#+BEGIN: collection-query-table"), read from
Vulpea\'s database) only changed when you ran
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "C-c C-x C-u"). New
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-collec-query-dblock-auto-mode") does that step
for you. It is #strong[off by default]: turn it on with
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "(sp-collec-query-dblock-auto-mode 1)").

- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "open"): a moment after visiting an Org file
  that has a block (idle timer, so opening is not slowed).
- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "save"):
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-collec-query-dblock-delay") (2 s) after any
  Org note is saved, every open buffer with a block is updated (gives
  Vulpea\'s autosync time to read the file).
- Only the #raw(lang:"verbatim", "collection-query-table") blocks (and
  the old #raw(lang:"verbatim", "vulpea-table") name) are touched, never
  clock tables; buffers without a block are skipped by a text search.
- No loops: an unchanged result leaves the buffer unmodified (compared
  by buffer hash); nothing is saved unless
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-collec-query-dblock-save") is set, and then
  only a buffer with no unsaved edits, and that save starts no new
  round.
- Also #raw(lang:"verbatim", "M-x sp-collec-query-dblock-update-all")
  for a one-off.

Docs: new section \"Keeping dynamic blocks up to date\" in
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "docs/tangles/funct/sp-collection-query-tables.org")\;
the #raw(lang:"verbatim", ".el") is tangled from it. CHANGELOG entry
