==== Summary
<summary>
The dashboard read every agenda file through Org at each start and
redraw. It now keeps each file\'s open TODOs in
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-cache-dir")
(#raw(lang:"verbatim", "dashboard-entries.eld")), keyed by path + mtime
\+ size.

- Only new or changed files are read at start; deleted files are
  dropped; the cache is dropped when
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "org-todo-keywords") changes.
- Deadline/scheduled are cached as absolute days and made relative on
  read, so they do not go stale overnight.
- A changed file is read from disk in a temp buffer (no mode hooks,
  nothing left open): #raw(lang:"verbatim", "org-map-entries") on a file
  name reuses an open buffer, which could put an older version in the
  cache. A buffer with unsaved edits is read instead and not cached.
- The per-draw #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-dashboard--entries-cache") and
  the public/private filtering in
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-dashboard--todos") are unchanged.
- Message:
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "[dashboard] read 100 agenda files: 99 cached, 1 re-read, in 0.01s").
- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "M-x sp-dashboard-clear-entries-cache") resets
  it.

==== Findings
<findings>
#strong[Coverage (100 agenda files from the running Emacs).]
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "org-map-entries") finds 362 keyword headings (339
open, 23 done). org-ql #raw(lang:"verbatim", "(todo)") finds the same
339 plus 3 TODOs under a #raw(lang:"verbatim", "* Archive :ARCHIVE:")
heading, which the dashboard skips on purpose; with
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "(not (tags \"ARCHIVE\"))") the two match exactly.
The file with its own #raw(lang:"verbatim", "#+TODO: OPEN | ANSWERED")
is read correctly by both. vulpea.db has only 35 todo rows (it indexes
only headings with an ID), so it cannot be the source.

#strong[Engine speed.] org-ql is not meaningfully faster: cold 2.5--3.4
s against 2.5--2.9 s for #raw(lang:"verbatim", "org-map-entries"),
almost all of it visiting the files. Warm it was 0.02--0.04 s against
0.05--0.07 s, possibly its own cache. The cache therefore keeps
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "org-map-entries") (no extra package).

