== Description
<description-223>
#emph[Requested by #strong[Sia] ·
#link("https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01BZHwSgnGAC4LTh4wgvYJsE?thread=cmsg_01BZHwSgnGAC4LTh4wgvYJsESgfFwDt41Q2LvPimo5EdKU")[project thread]]

Before: plugging the iPod into the Mac let Finder sync it straight away,
which read and deleted
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "iPod_Control/iTunes/Play Counts"), so Legacy
Scrobbler had nothing left to scrobble.

After: #raw(lang:"verbatim", "~/.config/listening/ipod-no-autosync")
turns that off and can undo it.

- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "on") (default, safe to rerun) sets
  `dontAutomaticallySyncIPods = true` in
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "com.apple.AMPDevicesAgent") (Finder\'s device
  sync helper, 10.15+) and #raw(lang:"verbatim", "com.apple.iTunes")
  (10.14 and earlier), then restarts
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "AMPDevicesAgent"). Earlier values are saved for
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "off").
- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "status") shows both settings, the agent,
  mounted iPods and whether #raw(lang:"verbatim", "Play Counts") is
  still on them.
- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "off") restores the values from before
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "on").
- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "backup") copies
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "Play Counts") +
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "iTunesDB") from every mounted iPod to
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "\u{24}XDG_DATA_HOME/listening/ipod-backups/"),
  skipping unchanged copies.
- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "agent install|remove") adds a launchd agent
  (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "StartOnMount")) that runs
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "backup") whenever a volume mounts.

The per-device Finder checkbox \"Automatically sync when this iPod is
connected\" is not changed by the script; the docs and
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "on") output say to untick it once.

How: bash 3.2--compatible script in
#raw(lang:"verbatim", ".config/listening/"), a new section in
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "PLAN.org"), and a CHANGELOG entry. Stacked on
\#171 because #raw(lang:"verbatim", "PLAN.org") only exists there.

Testing: run in a Linux container against stand-ins for
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "uname"), #raw(lang:"verbatim", "defaults"),
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "pgrep"), #raw(lang:"verbatim", "killall") and
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "/Volumes") (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "IPOD_VOLUMES")
override): on → on again (no-op) → backup ×2 (second skipped) → off
restored the original #raw(lang:"verbatim", "false") and removed the
unset key. #strong[Not run on a Mac]: whether current macOS still
honours the #raw(lang:"verbatim", "AMPDevicesAgent") key, whether Finder
reads Play Counts on connect even without syncing (the backup agent is
the fallback and may lose that race), and the launchd agent.

