Replaces the plain rendering of heading tags in Org buffers with SVG
chips from
#link("https://github.com/rougier/svg-tag-mode")[svg-tag-mode], driven
by the existing tag groups.

- #strong[Install]: #raw(lang:"verbatim", "use-package") with Elpaca,
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "svg-lib") from MELPA and
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "svg-tag-mode") from
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "rougier/svg-tag-mode").
- #strong[Colour]: each chip uses
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-org-tag-groups--chip-face"), so it takes the
  group colour from the theme-derived palette (\#249);
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "unsorted") tags are neutral (\#248). A theme
  change redraws the chips.
- #strong[Emoji]: the tag\'s emoji is shown in front of the chip in
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-org-tag-groups-select-emoji-face") (\#247),
  the same as #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-select-note").
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-org-svg-tags-show-emoji") turns it off.
- #strong[How]: #raw(lang:"verbatim", "svg-tag-mode") puts one display
  on one match, so there are three keywords: the tag name (chip), the
  colon before it (emoji) and the final colon (hidden). Matches outside
  the tags of a heading are ignored.
- #strong[Toggle / fallback]:
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "M-x sp-org-svg-tags-global-mode"), default from
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-org-svg-tags-enable"). In a terminal frame,
  or without SVG support, it stays off and the tags are plain text.
- #strong[Interactions]: stays off if
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "org-modern-tag") is on (it is nil in
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-org-appearance"));
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "org-indent") only sets a line prefix and
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "org-tags-column") is 0, so no alignment is
  needed.
- Edited the doc (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-org-tag-groups.org")) and
  re-tangled #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-org-tag-groups.el"). That also
  brings in #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-org-tag-groups--explicit-groups"),
