== Description
<description-307>
#emph[Requested by #strong[Sia] ·
#link("https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2WvunRxqLgBGFzjJ85aXPfJ")[project thread]]

==== Symptom
<symptom>
Caps Lock + number (focus, workspaces) works, but Caps Lock + Shift
combos (move window, move to workspace) do nothing, and with a text box
focused they type capitals.

==== Likely cause
<likely-cause>
The layer key (F18, from Caps Lock) is bound with
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "hs.hotkey.bind({}, \"f18\", ...)"). A hotkey only
matches the modifiers it is bound with, so F18 pressed while Shift is
already held is not that hotkey: the layer never opens, and Shift+letter
types a capital. Pressing Caps Lock first and Shift second would already
have worked, so this only breaks when Shift goes down first (or at the
same time).

==== Change
<change>
- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "aerospace-keys.lua"): the layer key is bound
  twice, with no modifiers and with #raw(lang:"verbatim", "shift"), both
  entering and leaving the same layer.
- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "aerospace.org"): one line saying the layer
  opens in either order.

==== Not run, and what to check
<not-run-and-what-to-check>
No Mac or Hammerspoon here, so this is a diagnosis from the code, not a
reproduced bug. After #raw(lang:"verbatim", "git pull") and a
Hammerspoon reload, try both orders: hold Caps, then Shift+=h= (move
left); and hold Shift, then Caps, then #raw(lang:"verbatim", "h"). If
Shift first still types capitals, the key events arrive another way and
I will switch the layer to an event tap that tracks F18 itself. No
CHANGELOG edit (nightly routine owns it).

