== Description
<description-308>
#emph[Requested by #strong[Sia]]

Caps Lock + number worked, but Caps Lock + Shift + key (move window /
move to workspace) did not, and typed capital letters in a text field.

Cause: the layer key (Caps Lock remapped to F18) was an
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "hs.hotkey") bound with no modifiers. Hammerspoon
matches those exactly, so with Shift already down F18 did not match,
passed through to the app, and the Shift+key then typed a capital
letter.

Fix
(#raw(lang:"verbatim", "hammerspoon/.config/hammerspoon/aerospace-keys.lua")):
the layer is now an #raw(lang:"verbatim", "hs.eventtap") that tracks F18
down/up whatever modifiers are held, swallows it, and looks the next key
up with or without Shift (Cmd/Alt/Ctrl pass through). The same bindings
are kept.

Only checked with #raw(lang:"verbatim", "luac -p")\; Hammerspoon is on
your machine. To test after merging:
