== Description
<description-310>
#emph[Requested by #strong[Sia] ·
#link("https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2WvunRxqLgBGFzjJ85aXPfJ")[project thread]]

==== Symptom
<symptom>
Caps+Shift+; enters AeroSpace\'s service mode, but there is no way back
out.

==== Likely cause
<likely-cause>
The service-mode #raw(lang:"verbatim", "esc") binding was
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "['reload-config', 'mode main']"). AeroSpace runs
the commands of a binding in order and stops at the first one that
fails, so if #raw(lang:"verbatim", "reload-config") fails (or reports an
error), #raw(lang:"verbatim", "mode main") never runs and the mode is
stuck. This is a diagnosis from the config, not a reproduced bug (no Mac
here).

==== Changes
<changes>
- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "aerospace.toml"):
  `esc = ['mode main', 'reload-config']` (leave first, then reload).
- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "aerospace-keys.lua"): Caps Lock + Esc runs
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "aerospace mode main"), so there is a way out
  even when AeroSpace does not receive Esc. It uses the existing
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "bind") helper, so it works with the current
  hotkey layer and with the event-tap version in \#310.
- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "aerospace.org"): kept in sync (the TOML block,
  the #raw(lang:"verbatim", "esc") note, the key list).

==== To check
<to-check>
After #raw(lang:"verbatim", "git pull"), a Hammerspoon reload and
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "aerospace reload-config"): enter service mode
with Caps+Shift+;, then try #raw(lang:"verbatim", "Esc"), then again and
try Caps+Esc. From Terminal,
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "aerospace mode main") always works. If neither
exits, the Hammerspoon Console or
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "aerospace reload-config") output will show the
real error; send it to me.

