== Description
<description-337>
Adds #raw(lang:"verbatim", "gh-pr-pdf"), a command that turns the pull
requests of a GitHub repository (and optionally its Discussions) into
searchable org files and one paginated PDF, so a codebase\'s history can
be studied as plain text.

```
gh-pr-pdf siainbuletin/dotfiles
```

==== Changes
<changes>
- New Stow package #raw(lang:"verbatim", "gh-pr-pdf/"): the script at
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "gh-pr-pdf/.local/bin/gh-pr-pdf") (links to
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "~/.local/bin/gh-pr-pdf")) and
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "gh-pr-pdf/README.org") (usage, needs, safety,
  \"Not run\"; Stow\'s default ignore list skips the README).
- The script wraps #raw(lang:"verbatim", "github-backup") for the raw
  JSON (description, conversation, reviews, inline review comments,
  commits), writes #raw(lang:"verbatim", "org/pr-NNNNN.org") per pull
  request in number order plus #raw(lang:"verbatim", "org/all.org"),
  then #raw(lang:"verbatim", "pandoc -t typst") and
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "typst compile") make the PDF.
  - Each org file has a property drawer
    (#raw(lang:"verbatim", ":PR_NUMBER:"),
    #raw(lang:"verbatim", ":STATE:"), #raw(lang:"verbatim", ":AUTHOR:"),
    #raw(lang:"verbatim", ":URL:")) for org-ql, and every commit is a
    link to #raw(lang:"verbatim", "github.com/OWNER/REPO/commit/\u{3c}sha>").
  - Options: #raw(lang:"verbatim", "--discussions"),
    #raw(lang:"verbatim", "--skip-fetch"),
    #raw(lang:"verbatim", "--no-pdf"),
    #raw(lang:"verbatim", "--per-pdf N"),
    #raw(lang:"verbatim", "--reverse"),
    #raw(lang:"verbatim", "--private"), #raw(lang:"verbatim", "-o DIR").
  - Pull request text comes from strangers, so raw HTML is dropped,
    #raw(lang:"verbatim", "pandoc") runs with
    #raw(lang:"verbatim", "--sandbox"), and lines starting with an org
    directive (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "#+INCLUDE:") and so on) become
    literal text. Checked with an injected
    #raw(lang:"verbatim", "#+INCLUDE: \"/etc/passwd\"").
- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "stow-migration/packages.tsv"): one row
  (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "gh-pr-pdf    all .local/bin/gh-pr-pdf")) so
  the package is in the list #raw(lang:"verbatim", "migrate.sh") derives
  for each machine. It matches no file in
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "\u{24}HOME"), so it should not change what the
  migration moves.

