==== Problem
<problem>
- BibTeX author #raw(lang:"verbatim", "Arthur, Christopher J.") gave the
  title #raw(lang:"verbatim", "J. Arthur (2022) Capital as...") instead
  of #raw(lang:"verbatim", "Arthur (2022) ...").

==== Cause
<cause>
- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-litnotes-titles--split-name") is the one
  function that finds the surname. The backfill
  (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-litnotes-meta--new-title")), titles
  report/convert and the BibTeX-authors path all call it.
- Names are flipped to #raw(lang:"verbatim", "First Last") before it
  runs, so it used its \"particle\" rule: lower-case words before the
  last word belong to the surname.
- That test ran with #raw(lang:"verbatim", "case-fold-search") on, so
  the initial #raw(lang:"verbatim", "J.") counted as a lower-case
  particle and went into the surname.

==== Change
<change>
- Particles are matched case-sensitively, and only whole lower-case
  words (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "van"), #raw(lang:"verbatim", "de la"))
  count.
- Commas are split outside braces only:
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "{Smith, Jones}, Ann") has surname
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "Smith, Jones")\;
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "Last, Jr., First") has surname
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "Last").
- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "{World Bank}") stays one surname; no comma and
  one word stays as is.
- Tests (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "tests/sp-litnotes-titles-test.el"),
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "tests/sp-litnotes-meta-test.el")): the forms
  above, #raw(lang:"verbatim", "case-fold-search") on and off, BibTeX
  authors, and the backfill title. 34/34 pass on Emacs 29.3 batch.
- No CHANGELOG edits.

==== Not tested
<not-tested>
- Not run on the real vault; existing litnotes already titled
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "J. Arthur (...)") are not renamed by this PR
  (re-run the titles convert/report to fix them).

