#raw(lang:"verbatim", "[fn::[[id:...][Concept]]]"), and ranks them.
Literate doc:
#raw(lang:"verbatim", "docs/tangles/academic/sp-see-also.org").

- #strong[Scanner] (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-see-also-parse-buffer")):
  finds inline footnotes with an #raw(lang:"verbatim", "id:") link and
  records the context of each: #raw(lang:"verbatim", "quote") or
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "prose"), and the open question heading above it
  (keywords come from #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-org-keywords-research"),
  so
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "QUESTION SCOPING READING SYNTHESIZING REVIEW")
  are open; #raw(lang:"verbatim", "STABLE ANSWERED DROPPED") are
  closed).
- #strong[No buffers visited]: files are read with
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "insert-file-contents") into a temp buffer in
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "fundamental-mode") (no hooks, no
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "org-mode"), no
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "org-element")). A test checks its footnote
  ranges against #raw(lang:"verbatim", "org-element"). Unsaved open
  buffers are read from the buffer.
- #strong[Cache]: per file, keyed by mtime and size, kept in
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "var/cache/see-also-index.eld")\; reset when the
  keywords change. Vulpea gives the litnote list, the titles, and (via
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "vulpea-db-query-links-to")) the files that link
  to a concept, so a concept lookup reads only those. The whole-vault
  index is the fallback.
- #strong[Priority]: two replaceable functions,
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-see-also-concept-score-function") and
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-see-also-question-priority-function").
  Default: mention weight (prose 1, quote 2, plus the keyword weight
  when under an open question), times
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "1 + ln(1 + other litnotes)").
- #strong[Dashboards]: a #raw(lang:"verbatim", "see-also") vulpea-ui
  widget (concepts by score, then open questions) and a
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "concept-usage") widget plus
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "#+BEGIN: concept-usage") dynamic block
  (litnote, where, under, context).

