#raw(lang:"verbatim", "tests/sp-reading-sidenotes-test.el").

- In #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-reading-mode"), each see-also footnote
  (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "[fn::[[id:...][Concept]]]")) shows as a small
  number in the text and as a Tufte-style sidenote in the right margin.
  The file is not changed (overlays only).
- Footnotes come from #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-see-also-parse-buffer")
  (\#366), no second parser.
- The note starts on the line of its number, wraps in the margin
  (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-reading-sidenote-margin"), 30 columns), and
  moves down if it would overlap the previous one. It is redone on
  window changes, text scale and edits (idle timer).
- Turns on/off with #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-reading-mode")
  (#raw(lang:"verbatim", "sp-reading-sidenotes")), or alone with
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "C-c w s"). The right margin is widened while it
  is on and restored afterwards. Narrow windows keep the plain
  footnotes.
- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "M-x sp-reading-sidenotes-export") exports the
  note with #raw(lang:"verbatim", "ox-tufte") (installed via
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "use-package") + Elpaca
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", ":ensure")) and opens the HTML.

==== Notes
<notes>
- #strong[Stacked on \#366] (base branch
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "claude/project-thread-7yi4nb")); retarget to
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "main") after it merges.
- #raw(lang:"verbatim", "ox-tufte") is an export backend, so it cannot
  draw in an Emacs window: the on-screen sidenotes use the Emacs margin
  display, and ox-tufte makes the matching HTML. It turns every inline
  footnote into a sidenote, not only see-also ones.
- The frame is not resized for the wider margin; the text column narrows
  instead.
- No CHANGELOG edits (nightly tidy).

==== Tested
<tested>
- 13 ERT tests (Emacs 29.3 batch, all pass): scanning through the
  parser, link text, margin line wrapping, overlay creation/removal, no
  overlap, narrow window, margin set/restore, following reading mode.
- A manual ox-tufte export of a footnote produced a
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "sidenote-number") label.
- Not seen in a real GUI frame: the actual look, wrapping, and
  #raw(lang:"verbatim", "vertical-motion") placement on screen are
  untried. The vault and DEVONthink are not involved.

